Article excerpt:
{{complex|date=November 2016}} '''Cognitive impairment''' (also called '''cognitive deficit''') is a condition in which cognitive functioning is altered.<ref>{{cite web|title=Cognitive Impairment|publisher=The Centers for Disease Control|url=https://www.cdc.gov/aging/pdf/cognitive_impairment/cogimp_poilicy_final.pdf|accessdate=Nov. 23, 2016}}</ref> The term "cognitive impairment" may mean deficits with global performance, like [[intellectual disability]] (also called "mental deficiency"). It may also mean specific deficits, such as [[learning disability]], slow learning or [[dyslexia]]. Cognitive impairment may be congenital or caused by environmental problems, such as brain injuries, neurological disorders or [[mental illness]]. ==References== <references/> [[Category:Disability]] {{biology-stub}}

