{{Infobox person/Wikidata|fetchwikidata=ALL}} '''Kaitlin Howarth''' (born 4 June 2000) is a [[New Zealand]] [[water polo player]]. She competed for the [[New Zealand women's national water polo team]] in the [[2019 World Aquatics Championships]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://waterpolo.sportresult.com/pdf/WCH2019/W39hr.pdf|title=18th FINA World Championships 2019 - Women's Water Polo - New Zealand|website=waterpolo.sportresult.com|access-date=2020-06-03|archive-date=2020-01-15|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200115064228/https://waterpolo.sportresult.com/pdf/WCH2019/W39hr.pdf|url-status=dead}}</ref> She played for [[Rangitoto College]], Murrays Bay Intermediate, North Harbour Water Polo Club, and Wasserfreunde Spandau 04. == References == <references /> ==Other websites == * [https://www.waterpolo.org.nz/news/volos-2017-new-zealand-into-top-twelve-with-crucial-10-9-win-ove/ new-zealand-into-top-twelve]{{Dead link|date=April 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }} * [https://www.sporty.co.nz/nhwp/About-1/Hall-of-Fame Hall-of-Fame] sporty.co.nz {{DEFAULTSORT:Howarth, Kaitlyn}} [[Category:2002 births]] [[Category:Living people]] [[Category:New Zealand water polo players]] {{sports-bio-stub}}

