{{cleanup}} お好み焼き is a Japanese dish consisting of a pan-fried batter cake and various ingredients. ''Okonomi'' means "what you like" or "what you want", and ''yaki'' means "grilled" or "cooked" (cf. ''yakitori'' and ''yakisoba''); thus, the name of this dish means "cook what you like". In Japan, okonomiyaki is mainly associated with Kansai or Hiroshima, but is widely available throughout the country. [[ca:Okonomiyaki]] [[de:Okonomiyaki]] [[en:Okonomiyaki]] [[es:Okonomiyaki]] [[fr:Okonomiyaki]] [[ko:오코노미야키]] [[id:Okonomiyaki]] [[it:Okonomiyaki]] [[ms:Okonomiyaki]] [[ja:お好み焼き]] [[pl:Okonomiyaki]] [[pt:Okonomiyaki]] [[ru:Окономияки]] [[fi:Okonomiyaki]] [[sv:Okonomiyaki]] [[zh:御好燒]]

