Article excerpt:
[[File:1983 Chevrolet Malibu.jpg|200px|thumb|a 1983 Chevrolet Malibu]] [[File:2017 Chevrolet Malibu (E2XX) front 3.25.18.jpg|200px|thumb|a 2017 Chevrolet Malibu]] The '''Chevrolet Malibu''' is a mid-size car that is manufactured by [[General Motors]]. There have been eight generations of the Malibu. The Malibu is named after the city in California, [[Malibu, California]]. The Malibu is sold in the [[United States]], [[Canada]], [[Mexico]], [[Brazil]] and the [[Middle East]]. The Malibu sucessed the 1997 Chevrolet Corsica/Beretta and was succeeded by the 1983 [[Chevrolet Celebrity]]. The eighth generation Malibu is a rebadged [[Daewoo]] Tosca, due to GM phasing out the brand. A ninth generation is being prepared for the 2016 market, it will be slightly larger and have a look similar to the Impala. ==Websites== * [http://www.chevrolet.com/malibu/ Chevrolet Malibu's Official website] {{Commonscat}} [[Category:Chevrolet automobiles]] [[Category:1960s automobiles]] [[Category:1970s automobiles]] [[Category:1980s automobiles]] [[Category:1990s automobiles]] [[Category:2000s automobiles]] [[Category:2010s automobiles]] [[Category:Sedans]] [[Category:Coupes]] {{Transport-stub}}
